the image of a man cursed to forever  hold the earth on his shoulders is one  that many of us may be familiar with but  how many of us actually know the story  behind the man the man this story  centers around is in fact not a man at  all but rather a Titan known as Atlas  and a common misconception is that it's  the earth on his shoulders but he was  actually cursed by Zeus to hold Uranus  the personification of the sky in the  heavens and that is what he bears on his  shoulders he was part of what many  considered to be the second generation  of titans being the son of the Titan II  a pitous and claim any one of the many  daughters of Oceanus making him the  brother to Prometheus Epimetheus and  many Oh tears it was also believed that  Atlas fathered many children a large  portion of them being regarded as nymphs  including the Hesperides Calypso and  Mayor the mother of homies which would  make the messenger called one of Atlas's  grandchildren during the war between the  Titans and the Olympians Atlas and his  brother many odious sided with the  Titans whereas Prometheus and Epimetheus  sided with Zeus but Atlas was believed  to have been one of the main sources of  rebellion against the Olympians  potentially even leading Titans into  battle which is why when the war ended  Zeus made an example of Atlas his  brothers and sisters were banished to  Tartarus but Zeus condemned that list to  stand on the western edge of the earth  and hold the heavens on his shoulders  forever separating Uranus and Gaia it's  because of this that Atlas is often  associated with endurance even sometimes  being called enduring Atlas a name that  is thought to embody his daily struggle  and eternal punishment Atlas was  regarded as the bearer of the heavens  and had a close link to astronomy when  sailors looked to the sky as a tool of  navigation it was their belief that they  were being instructed by Atlas and the  same can be said for farmers when they  attempted to measure the seasons the  roles of navigation and measuring the  seasons were somewhat combined as Atlas  became the God responsible for turning  the heavens on its axis causing the  Stars to rotate and revolve in Homer's  Odyssey Atlas is described as being  responsible for holding the pillars that  separated the heavens from the earth but  in Hesiod's Theogony  he's instead depicted as bearing the  weight of the heavens on his shoulders  the Atlas Mountains located in northwest  Africa in the regions of Morocco Algeria  and Tunisia are often heavily associated  of the Titan it's believed that when the  hero Perseus acquired the head of Medusa  he came across Atlas and when the Titan  glance into the Gorgons eyes he was  turned into an enormous mountain well  this story begins when Gaia gave the  goddess Hera a tree full of golden  apples as a wedding gift  the tree was guarded by alice's  daughters the Hesperides and was in a  location known by very few the titan was  told by an oracle that one day a son of  zeus would find the tree and attempt to  steal the golden apples that he sought  as guarded in order to stop this from  happening he would let no one enter his  land and when Perseus came across Atlas  he denied him any form of hospitality an  action that Perseus of course did not  take too kindly he lifted Medusa's head  above his shoulder showing the Titan and  immediately turned in Atlas into an  enormous mountain range a mountain range  that we now refer to as the Atlas  Mountains perhaps the most famous story  feature in atlas was the role he played  in the 12 labors of Heracles the Greek  hero was tossed by King Eurystheus to  steal some of the golden apples from the  gardens of asperities the apples were  guarded by the serpent night dragon  known as laDawn a foe that Heracles was  advised to avoid by Prometheus who  instead suggested that he asked the  Titan atlas for his assistance in return  for the Titans help  Heracles will take the burden of the  heavens from his shoulders when the  Titan eventually returned he refused to  resume his responsibilities as the  bearer of the heavens he planned to  leave Heracles with the weight of the  heavens on his shoulders by some form of  trickery Heracles convinced the Titans  to swap places under the illusion that  he could ease the strain on Alice's  shoulders but instead Heracles took the  apples and left just as Atlas planned to  leave him there are a few different  variations of the story relating back to  the depictions of Homer's Odyssey in  another variation of the story  Heracles built enormous pillars capable  of holding the heavens freeing Atlas  from his burden and in return the Titan  would acquire the golden apples for  Heracles  Atlas has quite an interest in and  symbolic figure and Greek mythology for  numerous reasons he symbolizes the  hardships that some of us have to endure  on a daily basis and he's stoic M  resilient approach show us that even the  most impossible task of holding the  entire weight of the heavens on one's  shoulders can be possible it's important  not to forget that he also symbolizes  the wrath of Zeus he was one of the main  forces opposing the rule of Zeus and as  a result he was made an extreme example  of warning anyone who dared to oppose  the rule of Zeus and his fellow  Olympians that a similar fate awaits  them it's likely that the ancient Greeks  looked at Atlas as an extremely useful  God he provided sailors of the means of  navigation and a way for farmers to  distinguish between the seasons if I had  to hazard a guess I'd believe that the  ancient Greeks were quite grateful  towards Atlas as many of them could have  believed that without the Titan there'd  be nothing to stop the heavens from  crashing down upon them quite often the  Titans are mentioned scarcely and even  less so after the war but Atlas is one  that we know quite a lot about compared  to the rest and it poses an interesting  question if the Titans would have won  the war would Atlas have assumed the  role similar to that of Zeus order now  it's heightened have challenged him I  look forward to hearing what you guys  think in the comments below as always  I've been your host mythology and  fiction explained  you  [Music]
 

